$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2,4-Dichlorophenylcarbamate (3) A 100-mL, round-bottomed flask
equipped with magnetic stirbar was charged with 1.51 g 2 (0.01 mol), 6.65
g NCS (0.05mol, 5 equiv), and 20mL MeCN. The mixture was refluxed for 12
h. After cooling, the mixture was poured into 250mL 5% Na2SO3, and a
solid precipitated. The solid was filtered on a coarse-porosity glass
frit and washed well with water. After air drying, the crude was
recrystallized from hexanes to give the title compound as colorless
needles (1.8 g, 82%). Methyl 2,4-Dichlorophenylcarbamate (3), yield (1.8
g, 82%). Mp 58-62 °C. δH (CDCl3): 8.12 (d, J=8.9Hz, 1H), 7.35 (d,
J=2.2Hz, 1H), 7.24 (dd, J=8.9 and 2.4Hz, 1H), 7.09 (bs, NH), 3.80 (s,
3H); δC (CDCl3): 153.67, 133.72, 128.92, 128.39, 128.12, 122.70, 120.81,
52.88. Elemental analysis calculated for C8H7Cl2NO2: C, 43.66; H, 3.21;
N, 6.37. Found: C, 43.84; H, 3.09; N, 6.32.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chlorination of aniline and methyl carbanilate by N-chlorosuccinimide and
synthesis of 1,3,5-trichlorobenzene
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Davis, Matthew C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2009), 39(6), 1100-1108

