$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-Chlorobenzofuran-3-carboxylate (1b). To a soln of methyl
benzofuran-3-carboxylate (0.18 g, 1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) at 25 °C, a soln
of NCS (0.13 g, 1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was added. The solution was heated
to 75 °C and stirred for 1 h. The mixture was concentrated and the
reaction was quenched with H2O (10 mL); the aqueous phase was extracted
with EtOAc (3 × 1 0 mL). The combined organic phase was washed
successively with H2O (10 mL) and brine (10 mL), dried overnight
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether-EtOAc). Yellow oil; yield:
0.18 g (82%); HPLC purity >99%. IR (KBr): 3447, 2953, 1756, 1561, 1236,
1065,782, 749 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.98 (s, 3 H, OCH3),
7.33-7.37 (m, 2 H, ArH), 7.44-7.47 (m, 1 H, ArH), 7.96-7.99 (m, 1 H,
ArH). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 51.3, 108.2, 110.4, 121.1, 124.1,
124.9, 125.2, 147.1, 152.7, 162.2. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 210 (33)
[M+], 179 (58), 145 (25), 83 (92), 57 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, MeCN as solvent gave very low yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Convenient chlorination of some special aromatic compounds using
N-chlorosuccinimide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gan, Zongjie; Hu, Bin; Song, Qiao; Xu, Yungen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2012), 44(7), 1074-1078

