$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Substrate 5 (100 mg, 0.487 mmol, 1 equiv), NCS (71.5 mg, 0.536 mmol, 1.1
equiv), and Pd(OAc)2 (8.4 mg, 0.024 mmol, 5 mol %) were combined in a 20
mL vial. CH3CN (4.0 mL) was added, the vial was sealed with a
Teflon-lined cap, and the mixture was heated at 100 °C for 12 h. The
solvent was removed under vacuum, and the resulting yellow/brown solid
was purified by chromatography on silica gel (Rf = 0.18 in 25% EtOAc/75%
toluene). Product 5-Cl was isolated as a light yellow solid (96 mg, 82%
yield); Product 5-Cl , Yield (96 mg, 82%). mp = 78.2- 79.2 °C. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.79-8.77 (m, 1H), 8.09 (s, 1H), 7.99 (s, 1H), 7.88
(d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.81-7.79 (multiple peaks, 2H), 7.74-7.71 (m, 1H),
7.56-7.48 (multiple peaks, 2H), 7.36-7.32 (m, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 156.75, 149.31, 136.11, 133.67, 131.85, 131.16, 129.67, 128.40,
128.25, 127.39, 126.70, 126.58, 125.21, 122.51. Two carbon resonances are
coincidently overlapping. HRMS electrospray (m/z ): [M+] calcd for
C15H10ClN, 239.0502; found, 239.0499. GC analysis (Restek Rtx@-5, FID
detector:100% integration.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
