$DATUM Solution of 10 (180 mg, 0.32 mmol) and NBS (180 mg, 0.97 mmol) in
pyridine (20 mL) was stirred for 4 hours at 50°C and then evaporated to
dryness. The residue taken up in DCM (50 mL) was washed with water (3 ×
20 mL). Drying over Na2SO4 the solvent was removed in vacuo. Purification
of the crude product was by column chromatography (20 g of silica gel,
DCM →DCM-MeOH, 9:1). 12a (170 mg, 0.27 mmol) as a white solid. Yield 82%.
m.p. 118-120°C; R f (A) 0.39; MS (ESI) m/z [M+H]+ calcd 634.1, 636.1;
found 634.3, 636.3.
