$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (a) With One Equivalent. To a stirred solution of
3-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone (4) [0.50 g, 2.25 mmol] in methanol (20
ml) was added N-bromosuccinimide (0.40 g, 2.26 mmol) at room temperature.
After 1 h, the methanol was evaporated in vacuo and water (25 ml) was
added. The resultant mixture was extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 25
ml) and the organic layers were separated, combined, dried (MgSO4), and
evaporated in vacuo. Chromatography on silica gel using dichloromethane
as eluent gave a solid, which was recrystallized from
dichloromethane:hexanes (2:1). 4-bromo-3-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone
(5a) as colorless crystals (0.55 g, 81%). mp. 101-102°C. IR: 3078, 1782,
and 1761 (sydnone C = O), 1622, cm-1. 1H-NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 7.02 (d, 2 H),
6.88 (s, 1 H), 3.83 (s, 6 H). 13C-NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 165.18 (sydnone C =
O), 160.92, 135.09, 104.01, 103.77, 86.31 (sydnone C-4), 56.00. Anal.
Calcd. for C10H9BrN2O4: C, 39.89; H, 3.01; N, 9.30. Found: C, 39.76; H,
2.94; N, 9.26.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, product depends upon the stoichiometry of the reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of 3-(3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Aleem, Amin S.; Turnbull, Kenneth
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2015), 47(1), 87-93

