$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2,5-Bis[2'-(5'-chlorothienyl)sulfanyl]thiophene (CTST). NCS
(2.14 g, 16 mmol) was added in small portions to a stirred solution of
2.50 g (8.00 mmol) of TST in acetic acid (12 mL) and dichloromethane (16
mL) over a period of 1.5 h at room temperature. The mixture was poured
into water (200 mL), and the organic layer was separated, washed with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution and water, dried over MgSO4, and
evaporated. The obtained solid was recrystallized from hexane to afford
white crystals. Yield: 2.60 g (80%).
2,5-Bis[2'-(5'-chlorothienyl)sulfanyl]thiophene (CTST), yield 2.60 g
(80%) mp: 58-59°C. FT-IR (KBr, cm-1): 1515, 1408, 1200, 1014, 1003, 960,
795, 563,536. 1H NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3, δ): 7.02 (d, 2H), 6.99 (s, 2H), 6.79
(d, 2H). 13C NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3/TMS, δ): 139.2, 133.9, 133.7, 132.5,
127.0. Anal. Calcd for C12H6Cl2S5: C, 37.79; H, 1.59. Found: C, 37.66; H,
1.78.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of highly refractive polyimides derived
from thiophene-containing aromatic diamines and aromatic dianhydrides
