$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Chlorination of Heterocycles Standard
Procedure: To a solution of heterocycle (0.1 mmol, 1.0 equiv.) in
chloroform (1.0 mL) at r.t. was added chlorinating reagent (CBMG or NCS,
0.12 mmol, 1.2 equiv.) with stirring. The reaction was monitored by thin
layer chromatography until completion. For substrates, which do not go to
completion in 12 hrs, acetonitrile was employed as the solvent. Upon
consumption of starting material, the reaction was concentrated and
directly purified by column chromatography on silica gel.
4-chloro-1-((2-chlorophenyl)diphenylmethyl)-1H-imidazole (11). Procedure:
Standard procedure was followed using 1.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform.
2,2,2-trichloro-1-(4-chloro-1H-pyrrol-2-yl)ethanone (16). Standard
procedure was followed using 2.2 equiv. of CBMG in chloroform at 50 °C
for 1 hr. 16 in 78% yield as a pale yellow solid. It is of note that the
R f of desired product co-spots with the starting material and could only
be distinguished by anisaldehyde3 stain (picture of tlc shown below for
clarity). m.p.: 116-118 °C; R f = 0.30 (10% ethyl ether/hexanes). 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.41 (brs, 1H), 7.28 (dd, J = 2.5, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.11
(dd, J = 3.0, 1.2 Hz, 1H) ppm; 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 172.9, 124.3,
122.0, 119.5, 115.5, 94.3 ppm; IR (neat) ν = 3314, 1656, 1432, 844, 747
cm-1; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calc’d for C6H4Cl4NO+ [M+H] 245.9042; found
245.9039.
