$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(2-Bromophenyl)-3-methylpyridine (S3). To a solution of
3-methyl-2-phenylpyridine (S1) (935 mg, 5.52 mmol, 1.00 equiv) in AcOH
(45 ml) in a pressure tube was added N-bromosuccinimide (NBS) (1.18 g,
6.62 mmol, 1.20 equiv) and Pd(OAc)2 (124 mg, 0.552 mmol, 0.100 equiv).
The reaction mixture was heated to 120 °C for 12 hours at which time the
reaction mixture was cooled to 23 °C and solvent was removed in vacuo.
The residue is purified by chromatography on SiO2 gel eluting with EtOAc
/ hexanes (3 : 7 (v/v)) to afford 1.10 g of the title compound (80%
yield) as a pale yellow oil. Rf = 0.48 (hexanes/EtOAc 1:1 (v/v)). 1H NMR
(600 MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 8.52 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (dd, J = 8.1
Hz, J = 1.0 Hz, iH), 7.60 (dd, J = 7.8 Hz, J = 0.7 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (dt, J =
7.5 Hz, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.30-7.24 (m, 3H), 2.16 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 158.55, 146.65, 141.50, 137.76, 132.62, 131.83,
130.22, 129.47, 127.47, 122.90, 122.54, 18.90. Mass Spectrometry:
HRMS-FIA (m/z): calcd for [C12H10BrN+H], 248.0069. Found, 248.0070.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, pressure tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
