$DATUM (a) With 0.5 Equivalent. To a stirred solution of hydrobromic acid (∼19%,
3 ml) was added 3-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl) sydnone (4) [0.075 g, 0.34 mmol]
and potassium bromate (0.028 g, 0.17 mmol) at room temperature. After 20
min, the precipitated solid was collected and washed with water.
Chromatography on silica gel using dichloromethane as eluent gave a
colorless solid, which was recrystallized from dichloromethane:hexanes
(2:1). 4-bromo-3-(2-bromo-3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone (5b) as colorless
microcrystals (0.101 g, 79%). mp. 194-196ºC. IR: 3093, 1765 (sydnone C =
O), 1581 cm-1. 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 7.29 (s, 1 H), 7.06 (s, 1 H), 4.00
(s, 3 H), 3.75 (s, 3 H). 13C-NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 164.97 (sydnone C = O),
160.31, 157.46, 133.94, 105.67, 103.38, 99.09, 87.45 (sydnone C-4),
57.20, 56.37. Anal. Calcd. for C10H8Br2N2O4: C, 31.61; H, 2.12; N, 7.37.
Found: C, 31.64; H, 2.18; N, 7.14.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, product depends upon the stoichiometry of the reagent,
alternative reaction conditions shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of 3-(3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Aleem, Amin S.; Turnbull, Kenneth
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2015), 47(1), 87-93

