$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chloro-6-methoxy-5-nitroquinoline (28). To a mixture of compound 27
(1.40 g, 6.86 mmol) and CH2Cl2 (22 mL) was added m-chloroperbenzoic acid
(1.77 g, 10.3 mmol) at 0°C. The reaction mixture was stirred at ambient
temperature overnight and washed with 10% sodium sulfite, saturated
NaHCO3, and saturated NaCl. The combined organic layer was collected and
evaporated to afford an oily residue. To the residue were added CH2Cl2
(33 mL) and phosphoryl chloride (6.4 mL), and the mixture was heated to
reflux overnight. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo, and the
residue was extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layer was
evaporated to give a residue that was purified by column chromatography.
Compound: 28. yield: 78%. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.07 (s, 3H), 7.50
(d, J= 8.9 Hz, 1H), 7.60 (d, J= 9.4 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (d, J= 8.9 Hz, 1H),
8.17 (d, J= 9.4 Hz, 1H).
