$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chloro-3-nitroaniline (4b). To a soln of 3-nitroaniline (1.38 g, 10
mmol) in DMF (15 mL) at 25 °C, a soln of NCS (1.34 g, 10 mmol) in DMF (15
mL) was added. The solution was heated to 75 °C and stirred for I h. The
mixture was concentrated and the reaction was quenched with H2O (10 mL);
the aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 30 mL). The combined
organic phase was washed successively with H2O (10 mL) and brine (10 mL),
dried overnight (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated. The residue was
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether-EtOAc).
yellow solid; yield: 1.33 g (77%). HPLC purity >98%. mp (free base) 94-95
°C (Lit. 96-97 °C). IR (KBr): 3204, 1628, 1526, 1352, 1319, 822, 789, 736
cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.40 (br s, 2 H, NH2), 6.77-6.96 (m, 1
H, ArH), 7.13-7.19 (m, 2 H, ArH). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 110.4,
114.1, 118.5, 127.3, 145.0, 149.1. HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for
C6H6ClN2O2: 173.0112; found: 173.0111.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, MeCN as solvent gave lower yield
