$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthetic procedure for 2-amino-5-chloro-3-methyl-benzoic acid (5)
2-amino-5-chloro-3-methylbenzoic acid (5) was prepared according to the
literature [14]. To a solution of 2-amino- 3-methylbenzoic acid (10 g, 66
mmol) in DMF (40 mL) was added N-chlorosuccinimide (8.8 g, 66 mmol) and
the reaction mixture was heated to 100 °C for 40 min. The reaction was
cooled to room temperature and left standing overnight. The reaction
mixture was slowly poured onto ice-water (150 mL), the resulting
precipitate was filtered and washed with water (3 × 50 mL) and then taken
up in ethyl acetate (600 mL). The ethyl acetate solution was dried over
magnesium sulfate, evaporated under reduced pressure and the residual
solidwaswashed with ether (3×30 mL) to afford intermediate
2-amino-5-chloro-3-methylbenzoic acid (5). White solid, yield 76.0%. m.p.
196-197 °C (dec.); 1H NMR (DMSO, 400 MHz), δ: 7.53 (s, 1H, Ph-H), 7.21
(s, 1H, Ph-H), 2.09 (s, 3H, CH3).
