$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of 3-(3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone (4) with Four Equivalents of
Potassium Chlorate. To hydrochloric acid (∼19%, 3 ml) was added
3-(3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone (4) [0.07 g, 0.32 mmol] and potassium
chlorate (0.16 g, 1.31 mmol) at room temperature with stirring. After 20
min, the precipitated solid was collected and washed with water.
Chromatography on silica gel using dichloromethane as eluent gave a
product, which was recrystallized from dichloromethane:hexanes (2:1).
4-chloro-3-(2,6-dichloro-3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone (5g) as colorless
microcrystals (0.08 g, 76%). mp. 256-258°C. 1H-NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 7.35 (s,
1 H), 4.08 (s, 6 H). 13C-NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ 162.52 (sydnone C = O),
155.38, 128.11, 110.08, 102.59, 99.79 (sydnone C-4), 57.59. Anal. Calcd.
for C10H7Cl3N2O4: C, 36.90; H, 2.17; N, 8.61. Found: C, 36.76; H, 2.16;
N, 8.37.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenation of 3-(3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)sydnone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Aleem, Amin S.; Turnbull, Kenneth
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Preparations and Procedures International (2015), 47(1), 87-93

